::  name       consent revoke field count
::  shape      fields - int (@u32)
::  invariant  a ConsentRevokeFact carries exactly seven fields (schema -
::             revoke_id - grant_id - holder_id - revoked_at - signer_id -
::             signature)
::  example    7
::  readers    Mantra - Glow Tend - Sur museum - Patchouli weave
::  nib        equinox-e208-mantra-tend-v0
::
::  Equinox e208 - Mantra M6 -- sixth Mantra structure pedestal in src/shape/.
::  Names ConsentRevokeFact's field count from mantra/src/consent_replay.rye,
::  the second growth milestone's revoke side: a revoke names the grant it
::  closes rather than restating its terms. Pedestal only; Rye still owns
::  refusal_grant's sibling revoke path and the orphaned-revoke refusal.
::
::  Seven sits under rune_shape.max_fields (15); this pedestal does not raise
::  it. Smaller than the nine-field grant by design -- a revoke identifies and
::  signs, and carries nothing of the grant's own terms forward.
+$  consent-revoke-field-count-shape
  $:  fields=@u32
  ==
